    "settings": {},
    "subgraphDefs": {
      "ks_aniso_spec": {
        "comments": [
          {
            "color": "#22d3ee",
            "id": "note_body",
            "position": {
              "x": 322,
              "y": 34
            },
            "size": {
              "h": 56,
              "w": 2378
            },
            "text": "**Kajiya–Kay** — with `T' = normalize(T + N·shift)` and half vector `H = normalize(L + V)`: `highlight = (1 − (T'·H)²)^(exponent/2)`.\nThe streak is perpendicular to the brushing direction and stretches along the surface — the signature look of brushed metal. Multiply by the light colour and `saturate(N·L)` outside."
          }
        ],
        "edges": {
          "h:out>th:b": {
            "from": {
              "node": "h",
              "port": "out"
            },
